title: Presidential Election
subtitle: Kornilov runs for re-election...
view-if: year = 1932 and (month = 4 or month = 5) and presidential_election_seen = 0
frequency: 1000
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: martov_campaign = 0; leuchtenberg_support_kornilov = 0; presidential_election_seen = 1; nts_candidate = "Leuchtenberg" if leuchtenberg_deported == 0 else nts_candidate = "Baidalakov";
tags: event
go-to: election_algorithm
set-jump: pres_election
face-image: img/presidentkornilov.jpg

@pres_election

The presidential election is coming up soon. [? if rsdrp_in_government = 0 : While the position of Chancellor is typically more important, recent governments have depended on the president's emergency decree powers, making the office vital. ?] [? if leuchtenberg_deported==0 : The Solidarists will run Leuchtenberg, while the RKP will run Kalinin. A victory for Leuchtenberg would lead us down a path of autocracy, and the beginning of an era of unspeakable horrors. ?][? if leuchtenberg_deported==1 : Since Leuchtenberg has been deported, the Solidarists will run Viktor Baidalakov in his stead. He is widely seen as a proxy for Leuchtenberg, who, despite his legal persecution, retains a popular base who wishes to see him returned to Germany. Meanwhile, the RKP will run Mikhail Kalinin. ?]
[? if rsrpi_formed: The RSRPI, our former leftists, are supporting Kalinin of the RKP, and will likely share an endorsement with the Communists. ?]

Many are calling for us to support the incumbent Kornilov, despite his well-known reactionary tendencies. Is he truly the best bulwark against Leuchtenberg's ascension? On the other hand, many in our party are calling for Yuliy Martov to run again, but he is reluctant.

[? if rkp_relation >= 50 : Another strange possibilty is an united front with the Communists, either to support Kalinin or our own candidate. ?]


- @support_kornilov: Support Kornilov.
- @support_martov: Run Yuliy Martov of the RSDRP.
- @support_kalinin: Support Mikhail Kalinin of the RKP.

@support_kornilov
subtitle: This is the default option.

Despite his known conservative nature, Kornilov has at least been keeping the Solidarists at bay. Thus, we must, reluctantly, support him.

- @final_election: The final vote...

@support_martov
subtitle: This will cost us 2 resources.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; martov_campaign = 1
go-to: martov_campaign

It takes effort to run a somewhat unexpected campaign. First, Martov has to be convinced to run, which shouldn't be too difficult. Then, we must convince the other parties to support Martov; *or not...*

The various minor leftist parties will likely support us, but who else will? Can we convince the Esers to support Martov? What about the Communists?


@support_kalinin
choose-if: rkp_relation >= 50 and reformist_strength < left_strength
unavailable-subtitle: [? if rkp_relation < 50 : We do not have good enough relations with the Communists, so they are not even willing to accept our support. ?] [? if reformist_strength >= left_strength : The reformist faction is able to dissuade the party from supporting this arrangement. ?]

Supporting Kalinin is rather unpopular in our party, even if the Communists accept our support. Are we sure?

- @support_kalinin_2: Yes, we will support Kalinin, despite the reformists' pleas against it.
- @support_martov: Support Martov instead.
- @support_kornilov: Support Kornilov instead.

@support_kalinin_2
on-arrival: rsdrp_support_kalinin = 1; reformist_dissent += 15; center_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 10; catholics_rsdrp -= 5; workers_rsdrp -= 3; rkp_relation += 10; communist_coalition += 2; z_relation -= 15; kadets_relation -= 15; musavat_relation -= 10

Fine. We have thrown our support to Chairman Kalinin of the RKP.

- @final_election: The final vote...

@martov_campaign

- @convince_psr: Convince the Esers.
- @convince_rkp: Convince the Radical Left.
- @convince_liberals: Convince the remaining liberals, wherever they are.
- @final_election: The final vote...

@convince_psr
choose-if: rsdrp_votes >= psr_votes
unavailable-subtitle: The Center knows that they are more popular than us; they do not see a reason to support our candidate.
on-arrival: {!
Q.psr_support_martov = 0;
if (Q.psr_relation >= 55 || (Q.psr_relation > 35 && Q.psr_party_leader == "Joos")) {
    Q.psr_support_martov = 1;
} else if (Q.psr_relation <= 35) {
    Q.psr_support_martov = 0;
} else {
    Q.psr_support_martov = 2;
}
!}
go-to: psr_failed if psr_support_martov = 0 or (psr_support_martov == 2 and historical_mode); psr_success if psr_support_martov = 1; psr_partial if psr_support_martov = 2 and not historical_mode
max-visits: 1

We remind the Center leaders of Kornilov's anti-Catholicism, and try to convince them that Kornilov's path will eventually lead to Leuchtenberg. We also remind them of the successes they've had as part of the Weimar coalition in Prussia with Yuliy Martov, and our support for the Center candidate Wilhelm Marx in the 1925 presidential election.

@psr_success
go-to: martov_campaign

The Center are convinced! They will be part of the Martov coalition.

@psr_partial

The Center are not satisfied with our arguments, but they are open to being convinced. They are willing to run a joint campaign if we front the resources.

- @pay_psr: Give them the resources they need.
- @martov_campaign: Forget about the Center.

@pay_psr
choose-if: resources >= 3
subtitle: -3 resources
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources (need 3)
on-arrival: resources -= 3; psr_support_martov = 1
go-to: martov_campaign

With our resources, the Center are convinced to support Martov over Kornilov.

@psr_failed
go-to: martov_campaign

Unfortunately, we fail to turn them away from Kornilov.

@convince_rkp
choose-if: rsdrp_votes >= rkp_votes
unavailable-subtitle: The RKP knows that they are more popular than us; they do not see a reason to support our candidate.
max-visits: 1

The RKP is supporting their own candidate, Mikhail Kalinin. [? if rkp_relation >= 50 : However, they are willing to be convinced to drop their campaign and support Martov; how do we convince them? ?][? if rkp_relation < 50 or rkp_party_leader != "Conciliators" : They do not seem willing to be convinced. ?]

- @rkp_resources: Use our resources.
- @rkp_relations: Use our good relations.
- @martov_campaign: Forget about the RKP.

@rkp_resources
view-if: rkp_relation >= 50 and not historical_mode
choose-if: resources >= 3
subtitle: -3 resources
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources (need 3).
on-arrival: resources -= 3; rkp_support_martov = 1
go-to: martov_campaign

The RKP now endorses Martov in the presidential election! We ask them to keep their support low-key, so as to not alienate the bourgeois voters.

@rkp_relations
view-if: rkp_relation >= 60 or (rkp_party_leader == "Conciliators" and rkp_relation >= 45)
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations are not good enough.
on-arrival: rkp_support_martov = 1
go-to: martov_campaign

The RKP now endorses Martov in the presidential election! We ask them to keep their support low-key, so as to not alienate the bourgeois voters.



@convince_liberals
max-visits: 1
go-to: convince_liberals_success if kadets_relation >= 50; convince_liberals_fail if kadets_relation < 50

The liberal vote ([+ musavat_name +] and DVP) has been falling over time, so they will probably be of minimal help to us. For what it's worth, the [+ musavat_name +] is already willing to support Martov.

@convince_liberals_success
on-arrival: kadets_support_martov = 1
go-to: martov_campaign

Thanks to our good relations, the DVP has promised to support Martov in the election.

@convince_liberals_fail
on-arrival: kadets_support_martov = 0
go-to: martov_campaign

We failed to convince the DVP to support Martov.



@final_election
on-arrival: election_round = 0
go-to: election_algorithm
set-jump: post_election


@post_election
on-arrival: {!
Q.martov_votes = 0;
Q.kornilov_votes = 0;
Q.leuchtenberg_votes = 0;
Q.kalinin_votes = 0;

// initial phase:
Q.leuchtenberg_votes += Q.nts_normalized;
Q.kornilov_votes += Q.other_normalized;
Q.kornilov_votes += Q.vs_normalized;

if (Q.martov_campaign) {
    Q.martov_votes += Q.rsdrp_normalized;
    Q.martov_votes += Q.musavat_normalized;
    if (Q.psr_support_martov && Q.psr_support_martov == 1) {
        Q.martov_votes += Q.psr_normalized;
    } else {
        Q.kornilov_votes += Q.psr_normalized;
    }
    if (Q.rkp_support_martov) {
        Q.martov_votes += Q.rkp_normalized;
        if (Q.rsrpi_formed && Q.rsrpi_votes) {
            Q.martov_votes += Q.rsrpi_normalized;
        }
    } else {
        Q.kalinin_votes += Q.rkp_normalized;
        if (Q.rsrpi_formed && Q.rsrpi_votes) {
            Q.kalinin_votes += Q.rsrpi_normalized;
        }
    }
    if (Q.kadets_support_martov) {
        Q.martov_votes += Q.kadets_normalized;
    } else {
        Q.kornilov_votes += Q.kadets_normalized;
    }
} else if (Q.rsdrp_support_kalinin) {
    Q.kalinin_votes += Q.rkp_normalized;
    Q.kalinin_votes += Q.rsdrp_normalized;
    Q.kornilov_votes += Q.psr_normalized;
    Q.kornilov_votes += Q.musavat_normalized;
    Q.kornilov_votes += Q.kadets_normalized;
} else {
    Q.kornilov_votes += Q.rsdrp_normalized;
    Q.kornilov_votes += Q.psr_normalized;
    Q.kornilov_votes += Q.musavat_normalized;
    Q.kornilov_votes += Q.kadets_normalized;
    Q.kalinin_votes += Q.rkp_normalized;
}
if (Q.leuchtenberg_support_kornilov) {
    Q.leuchtenberg_votes -= Q.nts_normalized;
    Q.kornilov_votes += Q.nts_normalized;
}

if (Q.kornilov_to_martov_bonus) {
    Q.kornilov_votes -= Q.kornilov_to_martov_bonus;
    Q.martov_votes += Q.kornilov_to_martov_bonus;
}
if (Q.kalinin_to_martov_bonus) {
    Q.kalinin_votes -= Q.kalinin_to_martov_bonus;
    Q.martov_votes += Q.kalinin_to_martov_bonus;
}

// check for majority
Q.kornilov_votes = Math.round(Q.kornilov_votes*1000)/10;
Q.martov_votes = Math.round(Q.martov_votes*1000)/10;
Q.leuchtenberg_votes = Math.round(Q.leuchtenberg_votes*1000)/10;
Q.kalinin_votes = Math.round(Q.kalinin_votes*1000)/10;

Q.kornilov_majority = (Q.kornilov_votes >= 50);
Q.kalinin_majority = (Q.kalinin_votes >= 50);
Q.leuchtenberg_majority = (Q.leuchtenberg_votes >= 50);
Q.martov_majority = (Q.martov_votes >= 50);
Q.any_majority = Q.kornilov_majority | Q.kalinin_majority | Q.leuchtenberg_majority | Q.martov_majority;

// check for plurality
Q.kornilov_plurality = (Q.kornilov_votes >= Q.leuchtenberg_votes && Q.kornilov_votes >= Q.martov_votes && Q.kornilov_votes >= Q.kalinin_votes);
Q.kalinin_plurality = (Q.kalinin_votes >= Q.kornilov_votes && Q.kalinin_votes >= Q.martov_votes && Q.kalinin_votes >= Q.leuchtenberg_votes);
Q.leuchtenberg_plurality = (Q.leuchtenberg_votes >= Q.kornilov_votes && Q.leuchtenberg_votes >= Q.martov_votes && Q.leuchtenberg_votes >= Q.kalinin_votes);
Q.martov_plurality = (Q.martov_votes >= Q.kornilov_votes && Q.martov_votes >= Q.leuchtenberg_votes && Q.martov_votes >= Q.kalinin_votes);
// If no candidate gets above 50%, then there's a second round. In the second round, a plurality wins. 
Q.election_round += 1;

// making the vote numbers nicer for the display
Q.kornilov_votes_disp = Q.kornilov_votes.toFixed(1);
Q.martov_votes_disp = Q.martov_votes.toFixed(1);
Q.leuchtenberg_votes_disp = Q.leuchtenberg_votes.toFixed(1);
Q.kalinin_votes_disp = Q.kalinin_votes.toFixed(1);
!}
go-to: kornilov_wins if kornilov_majority == 1; kalinin_wins if kalinin_majority == 1; leuchtenberg_wins if leuchtenberg_majority == 1; martov_wins if martov_majority == 1; no_majority_round1 if any_majority == 0 and election_round == 1; round2_results if election_round >= 2

Results:

Kornilov - [+ kornilov_votes_disp +]%

[+ nts_candidate +] - [+ leuchtenberg_votes_disp +]%

[? if rkp_support_martov == 0 : Kalinin - [+ kalinin_votes_disp +]% ?]

[? if martov_campaign > 0 : Martov - [+ martov_votes_disp +]% ?]

@no_majority_round1
on-arrival: leuchtenberg_support_kornilov = 1 if (martov_plurality or kalinin_plurality)
go-to: round2_menu

There is no majority in this round. In the second round, any candidate who wins a plurality will win overall. What should we do?

[? if martov_plurality or kalinin_plurality : In order to consolidate the vote for the Right, and to prevent a socialist from becoming president, [+ nts_candidate +] is no longer running in the second round, and has switched his endorsement to Kornilov. ?]


@round2_menu

- @round2_convince_z: Convince the Center to switch their support to us.
- @round2_convince_rkp: Convince the RKP to switch their support to us. 
- @round2_kornilov: Switch our support to Kornilov.
- @round2_kalinin: Switch our support to Kalinin of the RKP.
- @round2_vote: Let the second round voting begin.


@round2_convince_z
view-if: martov_campaign > 0 and psr_support_martov != 1 
choose-if: rsdrp_votes >= psr_votes
unavailable-subtitle: The Center knows that they are more popular than us; they do not see a reason to support our candidate.
on-arrival: {!
Q.psr_support_martov = 0;
// if Kornilov support is greater than Leuchtenberg and Martov support, this should be much harder

if ((Q.psr_relation >= 55 && Q.martov_votes >= Q.kornilov_votes) || (Q.psr_relation > 35 && Q.psr_party_leader == "Joos")) {
    Q.psr_support_martov = 1;
    if (Q.leuchtenberg_support_kornilov) {
        Q.kornilov_to_martov_bonus += Q.other_normalized/2;
    }
} else if (Q.psr_relation >= 50 && Q.leuchtenberg_support_kornilov) {
    Q.psr_support_martov = 1;
    Q.kornilov_to_martov_bonus += Q.other_normalized/2;
} else if (Q.psr_relation <= 35 || (Q.psr_relation <= 45 && Q.martov_votes < Q.kornilov_votes && Q.kornilov_votes > Q.leuchtenberg_votes && Q.difficulty >= 0)) {
    Q.psr_support_martov = 0;
} else {
    Q.psr_support_martov = 2;
}
!}
go-to: r2_psr_failed if psr_support_martov = 0 or (psr_support_martov = 2 and historical_mode); r2_psr_success if psr_support_martov = 1; r2_psr_partial if psr_support_martov = 2 and not historical_mode
max-visits: 1

@r2_psr_success
go-to: round2_menu
on-departure: leuchtenberg_support_kornilov = 1 if martov_votes + psr_votes > leuchtenberg_votes

[? if leuchtenberg_support_kornilov : The Center's opinion is affected by the Solidarist's support of Kornilov, and is willing to turn away from him. ?] The Center are convinced! They will be part of the Martov coalition. [? if leuchtenberg_support_kornilov : In addition, they will also bring in some minor parties who will support us. ?]

[? if not leuchtenberg_support_kornilov and martov_votes + psr_votes > leuchtenberg_votes: With the Center Party supporting Martov, [+ nts_candidate +] has dropped out of the race, and the Solidarists have endorsed Kornilov to prevent a socialist from becoming president. ?]

@r2_psr_partial

The Center are not satisfied with our arguments, but they are open to being convinced[? if leuchtenberg_support_kornilov: , especially given the Solidarist's support for Kornilov. ?]. They are willing to run a joint campaign if we front the resources.

- @r2_pay_psr: Give them the resources they need.
- @round2_menu: Forget about the Center.

@r2_pay_psr
choose-if: resources >= 2
subtitle: -2 resources
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources (need 2)
on-arrival: resources -= 2; psr_support_martov = 1
on-departure: leuchtenberg_support_kornilov = 1 if martov_votes + psr_votes > leuchtenberg_votes
go-to: round2_menu

With our resources, the Center are convinced to support Martov over Kornilov.

[? if not leuchtenberg_support_kornilov and martov_votes + psr_votes > leuchtenberg_votes: With the Center Party supporting Martov, [+ nts_candidate +] has dropped out of the race, and the Solidarists have endorsed Kornilov to prevent a socialist from becoming president. ?]

@r2_psr_failed
go-to: round2_menu

Unfortunately, we fail to turn them away from Kornilov. [? if kornilov_votes > martov_votes : Given that Kornilov received more votes than Martov, they believe that we should support the incumbent President, not the other way around. ?]




@round2_convince_rkp
